From 3dcf60c1a69644a714e84779817fcce062d9724b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:13:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2357/2368] media: qcom: camss: icp: add the HFI queue layer
 and build the ICP alone

The ICP RFC calls an HFI layer (camss-icp-hfi.c) that it does not carry,
and its Makefile names a BPS command builder that is missing too, so the
series does not build. Add the HFI part the ICP needs to come up:
memory (shared, QDSS, firmware-uncached carved into secondary heap,
queue table, command/message/debug rings and the failure-reason buffer),
the queue table in interrupt mode as the firmware expects it, command
writes with the doorbell, message and debug queue readers, and the
system bring-up: SYS_INIT, the debug level, a ping.

Build only the ICP module for now; BPS and IPE need the pieces that are
still missing. Accept a firmware-name with an extension so a single-file
signed .mbn loads as is, and clean up the warnings in camss-icp.c.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit f73ae51e87d37ac9de5ee8018f7a7573fd40662b)

